# Sync gates (pointer)

State drift is the number one workflow pain. Enforcement is layered:

| Layer | Mechanism | What |
|---|---|---|
| Inline capture | `ba-context-capture` (every turn) | New facts/decisions → SESSION-CONTEXT.md, silent |
| Deterministic breakpoints | `stop` + `preCompact` hooks (`inject-state-reminder.py --stop`, `snapshot-before-compact.py`) | Unpromoted-item count + staleness computed from files, injected only when real |
| Judgement breakpoints | This pointer | The triggers below — run the procedure from the reference |

**Triggers that MUST run a quick sync check:** after a debrief completes · before switching initiatives · before any Confluence publish · on `/validate-state` (writes this chat into initiative files + ba-actions) · on `/wrap` (chat-only checkpoint).

**Procedures** (check steps, sync card format, auto-promotion rules): load `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/references/sync-procedures.md` when a trigger fires or `/validate-state` runs. `/validate-state` checks this chat against the current initiative. Write what this chat captured into the right files: `SESSION-CONTEXT.md`, the tracker, and `status-data.json` where those files already exist, and upsert only the BA actions that came from this chat into `~/.cursor/_workstream/ba-actions.json`. Do not refresh the workboard. Do not walk every open action. Do not invent files. If something has no obvious home, say so and ask.

**`/wrap`** follows `~/.cursor/commands/wrap.md` only (do not open `sync-procedures.md` for it). It is a chat-only checkpoint and does not refresh the workboard.

**End of day** is `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/references/eod-closeout-procedure.md`, loaded only when `/workboard end-of-day` fires.

Canonical file hierarchy on conflict: tracker > status-data > SESSION-CONTEXT > everything else (full ownership table: `ba-assistant/SKILL.md`).

`/wrap` must include **sync-ba-actions** for any action created or changed in this chat (see `commands/wrap.md` step 3). Print `Gate: ba-actions-sync: PASS/FAIL`.

`/sync-check` is retired — treat as `/validate-state`.
